<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Abecafe ups 1997/98 coffee estimate.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Abecafe ups 1997/98 coffee estimate.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop should reach 24 million 60-kg bags, up from a previous forecast in February of 23.2 million bags, said Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Association (Abecafe).</p>
<p>Of the total, 19.5 million bags are forecast to be of arabica coffee and 4.5 million bags of robusta against February figures of 18.7 million and 4.5 million bags, respectively.  </p>
<p>The forecast was reached after a survey of 22 of the 45 companies which belong to Abecafe. The 22 companies represent 85 percent of Abecafe's total exports, the association said.</p>
<p>In February, 23 Abecafe members participated in the survey.</p>
<p>No figure was given for the 1996/97 crop.</p>
<p>A breakdown by state for arabica in million bags follows.  </p>
<p>				    MAY EST	   FEB EST</p>
<p>    Minas Gerais		    11.10	     10.55</p>
<p>    Espirito Santo		   1.10		1.15</p>
<p>    Sao Paulo			  2.85		2.75</p>
<p>    Parana			     2.65		2.40</p>
<p>    Bahia				0.95		0.95</p>
<p>    Rondonia			   0.10		0.10</p>
<p>    Other				0.75		0.80</p>
<p>A breakdown by state for conillon in million bags follows.</p>
<p>				   MAY EST	   FEB EST</p>
<p>    Minas Gerais		     0.10		0.10</p>
<p>    Espirito Santo		   2.90		3.00</p>
<p>    Bahia				0.25		0.20</p>
<p>    Rondonia			   1.15		1.10</p>
<p>    Others			     0.10		0.10</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
